{"question": "Rank the ten busiest district courts by weighted filings per judgeship in FY2025.", "record": {"question_id": "ts-compare-top-districts", "answerer": "claude-code-sonnet", "final_text": "The ten busiest district courts by weighted total filings per judgeship in FY2025 (JB-2025, Table X-1A; national figure 534 (JB-2025), later revised to 493 (JFF-2025)):\n\n| Rank | Court | Weighted Filings/Judgeship |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | D.S.C. | 1,161 |\n| 2 | E.D.N.C. | 989 |\n| 3 | D.N.J. | 974 |\n| 4 | E.D. Tex. | 894 |\n| 5 | E.D. Cal. | 887 |\n| 6 | W.D. Tex. | 818 |\n| 7 | N.D. Ill. | 797 |\n| 8 | N.D. Ga. | 775 |\n| 9 | D. Ariz. | 772 |\n| 10 | C.D. Cal. | 759 |\n\nAll ten exceed the 430 threshold the Judicial Conference generally uses in considering new judgeships, and several exceed the 600 judicial-emergency threshold.", "tool_calls": [{"name": "compare_courts", "arguments": {"measure": "weighted_total_filings_per_judgeship", "fiscal_year": 2025, "top_n": 10}, "output": {"status": "ok", "data": {"measure": "weighted_total_filings_per_judgeship", "measure_label": "Weighted total filings per judgeship", "unit": "weighted filings per judgeship", "fiscal_year": 2025, "edition": "JB-2025", "table_code": "X-1A", "order": "desc", "rows": [{"rank": 1, "court": "SC", "court_name": "South Carolina", "citation": "D.S.C.", "value": 1161, "cell_ref": "Table X-1A!G27"}, {"rank": 2, "court": "NC-E", "court_name": "North Carolina, Eastern", "citation": "E.D.N.C.", "value": 989, "cell_ref": "Table X-1A!G24"}, {"rank": 3, "court": "NJ", "court_name": "New Jersey", "citation": "D.N.J.", "value": 974, "cell_ref": "Table X-1A!G19"}, {"rank": 4, "court": "TX-E", "court_name": "Texas, Eastern", "citation": "E.D. Tex.", "value": 894, "cell_ref": "Table X-1A!G38"}, {"rank": 5, "court": "CA-E", "court_name": "California, Eastern", "citation": "E.D. Cal.", "value": 887, "cell_ref": "Table X-1A!G70"}, {"rank": 6, "court": "TX-W", "court_name": "Texas, Western", "citation": "W.D. Tex.", "value": 818, "cell_ref": "Table X-1A!G40"}, {"rank": 7, "court": "IL-N", "court_name": "Illinois, Northern", "citation": "N.D. Ill.", "value": 797, "cell_ref": "Table X-1A!G50"}, {"rank": 8, "court": "GA-N", "court_name": "Georgia, Northern", "citation": "N.D. Ga.", "value": 775, "cell_ref": "Table X-1A!G94"}, {"rank": 9, "court": "AZ", "court_name": "Arizona", "citation": "D. Ariz.", "value": 772, "cell_ref": "Table X-1A!G68"}, {"rank": 10, "court": "CA-C", "court_name": "California, Central", "citation": "C.D. Cal.", "value": 759, "cell_ref": "Table X-1A!G71"}], "national": {"value": 534, "edition": "JB-2025", "table_code": "X-1A", "url": "https://www.uscourts.gov/sites/default/files/document/jb_x1a_0930.2025.xlsx", "cell_ref": "Table X-1A!G5"}, "national_latest": {"value": 493, "edition": "JFF-2025", "table_code": "6.2", "url": "https://www.uscourts.gov/sites/default/files/document/jff_6.2_0930.2025.xlsx", "cell_ref": "Table 6.2!C4"}, "not_published": [], "total_courts": 91}, "clarification": null, "provenance": [{"source": "official_table", "table_code": "X-1A", "series": "Judicial Business of the United States Courts", "edition": "JB-2025", "period": {"fiscal_year": 2025, "period_end": "2025-09-30", "period_type": "fiscal_year"}, "definition": "Weighted civil plus weighted criminal plus weighted supervised release hearings, divided by authorized judgeships. The Judicial Conference generally considers new judgeships above 430 and treats above 600 as a judicial emergency threshold (see CRS Insight IN12541).", "url": "https://www.uscourts.gov/sites/default/files/document/jb_x1a_0930.2025.xlsx", "cell_ref": null, "revision_status": null, "first_published": null, "later_revisions": [], "reconciliation": null, "dataset_release": null, "note": "All 91 values from JB-2025 Table X-1A."}], "warnings": [{"code": "revised_figure", "message": "Court values are only published in JB-2025. The national figure in that edition is 534; JFF-2025 later revised it to 493. Compare courts with the JB-2025 national figure, not the revised one.", "severity": "caution"}], "suggested_next": []}, "error": null, "latency_s": null}], "extra_outputs": [], "cited_figures": [], "behavior": null, "latency_s": 6.252, "input_tokens": 4, "output_tokens": 500, "error": null}, "score": {"question_id": "ts-compare-top-districts", "suite": "tool_selection", "split": "test", "tags": ["compare"], "correct": true, "checks": {"behavior": true, "tools": true}, "expected_behavior": "answer", "actual_behavior": "answer", "error_category": null, "notes": [], "latency_s": 6.252}}
{"question": "Compare civil filings per judgeship in S.D.N.Y., E.D.N.Y. and D.N.J. for FY2024.", "record": {"question_id": "ts-compare-named-districts", "answerer": "claude-code-sonnet", "final_text": "For FY2024, civil filings per judgeship (unweighted, Table X-1A, JB-2024):\n\n| Rank | District | Civil filings/judgeship |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | D.N.J. | 699 |\n| 2 | E.D.N.Y. | 597 |\n| 3 | S.D.N.Y. | 362 |\n\nNational average: 412 (JB-2024) \u2014 note JFF-2024 later revised the national figure to 411, but the court-level figures above are only published in JB-2024, so I'm comparing against the JB-2024 national number.\n\nD.N.J. carries nearly double the caseload per judge of S.D.N.Y., with E.D.N.Y. in between and above the national average. Let me know if you'd instead like the **weighted** civil filings per judgeship, which accounts for case complexity rather than raw counts.", "tool_calls": [{"name": "compare_courts", "arguments": {"courts": ["NY-S", "NY-E", "NJ"], "measure": "civil_filings_per_judgeship", "fiscal_year": 2024}, "output": {"status": "ok", "data": {"measure": "civil_filings_per_judgeship", "measure_label": "Civil filings per judgeship (unweighted)", "unit": "filings per judgeship", "fiscal_year": 2024, "edition": "JB-2024", "table_code": "X-1A", "order": "desc", "rows": [{"rank": 1, "court": "NJ", "court_name": "New Jersey", "citation": "D.N.J.", "value": 699, "cell_ref": "Table X-1A!D19"}, {"rank": 2, "court": "NY-E", "court_name": "New York, Eastern", "citation": "E.D.N.Y.", "value": 597, "cell_ref": "Table X-1A!D14"}, {"rank": 3, "court": "NY-S", "court_name": "New York, Southern", "citation": "S.D.N.Y.", "value": 362, "cell_ref": "Table X-1A!D15"}], "national": {"value": 412, "edition": "JB-2024", "table_code": "X-1A", "url": "https://www.uscourts.gov/sites/default/files/2025-01/jb_x1a_0930.2024.xlsx", "cell_ref": "Table X-1A!D5"}, "national_latest": {"value": 411, "edition": "JFF-2024", "table_code": "6.2", "url": "https://www.uscourts.gov/sites/default/files/document/jff_6.2_0930.2024.xlsx", "cell_ref": "Table 6.2!H5"}, "not_published": [], "total_courts": 3}, "clarification": null, "provenance": [{"source": "official_table", "table_code": "X-1A", "series": "Judicial Business of the United States Courts", "edition": "JB-2024", "period": {"fiscal_year": 2024, "period_end": "2024-09-30", "period_type": "fiscal_year"}, "definition": "Civil cases filed divided by authorized judgeships. Excludes civil cases reopened, remanded, or transferred to the district by order of the Judicial Panel on Multidistrict Litigation.", "url": "https://www.uscourts.gov/sites/default/files/2025-01/jb_x1a_0930.2024.xlsx", "cell_ref": null, "revision_status": null, "first_published": null, "later_revisions": [], "reconciliation": null, "dataset_release": null, "note": "All 3 values from JB-2024 Table X-1A."}], "warnings": [{"code": "revised_figure", "message": "Court values are only published in JB-2024. The national figure in that edition is 412; JFF-2024 later revised it to 411. Compare courts with the JB-2024 national figure, not the revised one.", "severity": "caution"}], "suggested_next": []}, "error": null, "latency_s": null}], "extra_outputs": [], "cited_figures": [], "behavior": null, "latency_s": 11.971, "input_tokens": 4, "output_tokens": 1064, "error": null}, "score": {"question_id": "ts-compare-named-districts", "suite": "tool_selection", "split": "test", "tags": ["compare"], "correct": true, "checks": {"behavior": true, "tools": true}, "expected_behavior": "answer", "actual_behavior": "answer", "error_category": null, "notes": [], "latency_s": 11.971}}
