{"question": "Break down the change in civil terminations from FY2023 to FY2024 by district and case type.", "record": {"question_id": "ts-explain-change-terminations", "answerer": "claude-code-sonnet", "final_text": "## Civil Terminations: FY2023 \u2192 FY2024\n\n**National change:** 293,677 (JB-2023) \u2192 396,635 (JB-2024), an increase of **+102,958 (+35.1%)**.\n\n### By District (top contributors, IDB-derived breakdown)\n| District | FY2023 | FY2024 | Change | Share of total change |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| N.D. Fla. | 37,047 | 141,214 | **+104,167** | 101% |\n| S.D. Fla. | 21,450 | 8,730 | -12,720 | -12% |\n| N.D. Cal. | 6,499 | 10,342 | +3,843 | +4% |\n| D.S.C. | 3,275 | 6,750 | +3,475 | +3% |\n| N.D. Ill. | 8,103 | 10,710 | +2,607 | +3% |\n| N.D. Ga. | 9,493 | 7,039 | -2,454 | -2% |\n| D.N.H. | 702 | 2,626 | +1,924 | +2% |\n| C.D. Cal. | 14,859 | 16,479 | +1,620 | +2% |\n| D. Vt. | 312 | 1,337 | +1,025 | +1% |\n| W.D. La. | 4,514 | 3,708 | -806 | -1% |\n| All other (84 districts) | 187,423 | 187,700 | +277 | ~0% |\n\n### By Case Type (IDB-derived)\n| Case Type | FY2023 | FY2024 | Change | Share of total change |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Personal Injury/Product Liability | 66,651 | 161,653 | **+95,002** | 92% |\n| Civil Rights | 39,846 | 43,148 | +3,302 | 3% |\n| Prisoner Petitions | 51,661 | 49,013 | -2,648 | -3% |\n| Insurance | 15,904 | 17,927 | +2,023 | 2% |\n| Immigration | 9,754 | 11,763 | +2,009 | 2% |\n| Other Contract Actions | 11,002 | 12,383 | +1,381 | 1% |\n| Intellectual Property Rights | 13,217 | 14,206 | +989 | 1% |\n| Other Personal Injury | 19,229 | 19,824 | +595 | 1% |\n| Consumer Credit | 8,355 | 8,790 | +435 | ~0% |\n| Labor Laws | 13,472 | 13,110 | -362 | ~0% |\n| All other (26 types) | 44,586 | 44,818 | +232 | ~0% |\n\n### Main driver\nThis increase is almost entirely **multidistrict litigation (MDL)** activity: MDL terminations changed by **+97,266 (94% of the total change)**. The single largest factor is **N.D. Fla. MDL 2885** (3M combat earplugs), whose Personal Injury/Product Liability terminations rose from 35,263 to 139,486 (**+104,223**, itself exceeding the entire national change). Partially offsetting this, **S.D. Fla. MDL 2924** terminations fell by 12,699.\n\nNote the N.D. Fla. district total exceeds 100% of the national change; other districts' net movements (mostly small MDL-related shifts and offsets like S.D. Fla.) combine with it to net back to the actual national total. (This MDL breakdown is *idb_derived*, not an official Table C-1 line item.)", "tool_calls": [{"name": "explain_change", "arguments": {"measure": "civil_cases_terminated", "court": "US", "period_from": 2023, "period_to": 2024}, "output": {"status": "ok", "data": {"measure": "civil_cases_terminated", "measure_label": "Civil cases terminated", "unit": "cases", "court": "US", "court_name": "All district courts", "period_from": 2023, "period_to": 2024, "mode": "count", "headline": "Civil cases terminated for All district courts rose by 102,958 from FY2023 to FY2024. Largest contributors (IDB): N.D. Fla. +104,167.", "official_from": {"value": 293677, "edition": "JB-2023", "table_code": "C-1", "url": "https://www.uscourts.gov/sites/default/files/data_tables/jb_c1_0930.2023.xlsx", "cell_ref": "Report C-1!C6"}, "official_to": {"value": 396635, "edition": "JB-2024", "table_code": "C-1", "url": "https://www.uscourts.gov/sites/default/files/2024-12/jb_c1_0930.2024.xlsx", "cell_ref": "Report C-1!C5"}, "official_change": 102958, "official_change_pct": 0.35058244261552657, "idb_from": 293677, "idb_to": 396635, "idb_change": 102958, "idb_change_excluding_mdl_direct": null, "filings_effect": null, "judgeship_effect": null, "decomposition_series": "Totals: Table C-1 (JB-2023, JB-2024). Breakdowns: FJC IDB civil records.", "by_district": [{"key": "FL-N", "label": "N.D. Fla.", "value_from": 37047, "value_to": 141214, "change": 104167, "share_of_change": 1.011742652343674, "key_contributor": true}, {"key": "FL-S", "label": "S.D. Fla.