{"question": "What was the median time to disposition for Social Security appeals filed in FY2022 in the Ninth Circuit's districts?", "record": {"question_id": "ts-cohort-median-time", "answerer": "claude-code-sonnet", "final_text": "Based on FJC Integrated Database case-level records (not a published Judicial Facts and Figures table), for Social Security Laws cases (nos group covering codes 861\u2013865) filed in FY2022 across the Ninth Circuit's district courts:\n\n**Circuit-wide:** median 283 days (95% CI 274\u2013292), n=3,263\n\n**By district:**\n| District | n | Median days | 95% CI |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| C.D. Cal. | 692 | 311 | 302\u2013323 |\n| E.D. Wash. | 514 | 43.5 | 33\u201378 |\n| W.D. Wash. | 508 | 204.5 | 196\u2013210 |\n| E.D. Cal. | 459 | 366 | 335\u2013400 |\n| D. Ariz. | 335 | 392 | 363\u2013411 |\n| D. Or. | 312 | 415.5 | 392\u2013443 |\n| N.D. Cal. | 139 | 301 | 251\u2013368 |\n| S.D. Cal. | 89 | 399 | 267\u2013464 |\n| D. Nev. | 87 | 246 | 209\u2013281 |\n| D. Idaho | 54 | 391 | 331\u2013442 |\n| D. Mont. | 31 | 336 | 237\u2013470 |\n| D. Alaska | 28 | 190 | 170\u2013283 *(caution: <30 cases)* |\n| D. Hawaii | 15 | 242 | 171\u2013359 *(caution: <30 cases)* |\n\nGuam and N. Mariana Islands had no matching cases. E.D. Wash. stands out as a striking outlier (median ~44 days) \u2014 worth flagging if that's central to your analysis, since it's far below every other district in the circuit.", "tool_calls": [{"name": "find_cases", "arguments": {"courts": ["CIR-09"], "fy_from": 2022, "fy_to": 2022, "nos_groups": ["Social Security Laws"]}, "output": {"status": "ok", "data": {"handle": "coh_8900a2d5a128", "parent": null, "spec": {"courts": ["AK", "AZ", "CA-C", "CA-E", "CA-N", "CA-S", "GU", "HI", "ID", "MP", "MT", "NV", "OR", "WA-E", "WA-W"], "fy_from": 2022, "fy_to": 2022, "nos_groups": ["Social Security Laws"]}, "basis": "filed", "n": 3263, "by_fiscal_year": [{"key": "2022", "n": 3263, "share": 1}], "top_courts": [{"key": "CA-C", "n": 692, "share": 0.