{"question": "Does the IDB reproduce the official count of civil cases filed nationally in FY2023?", "record": {"question_id": "ts-reconcile-figure", "answerer": "claude-code-sonnet", "final_text": "Yes \u2014 the IDB rebuild closely matches the official count for FY2023 civil cases filed nationally:\n\n- **Official (Table C-1):** 339,731 (JB-2023)\n- **IDB rebuild:** 339,965\n- **Variance:** 234 cases (0.07%), well within the tolerance threshold\n\nStatus: **matched**. No specific explanation was needed since the variance is negligible (rounding/timing noise typical of independent case-by-case rebuilds).", "tool_calls": [{"name": "reconcile", "arguments": {"measure": "civil_cases_filed", "court": "US", "fiscal_year": 2023}, "output": {"status": "ok", "data": {"measure": "civil_cases_filed", "measure_label": "Civil cases filed", "court": "US", "court_name": "All district courts", "fiscal_year": 2023, "official": {"value": 339731, "edition": "JB-2023", "table_code": "C-1", "url": "https://www.uscourts.gov/sites/default/files/data_tables/jb_c1_0930.2023.xlsx", "cell_ref": "Report C-1!B6"}, "official_editions": [{"value": 339731, "edition": "JB-2023", "table_code": "C-1", "url": "https://www.uscourts.gov/sites/default/files/data_tables/jb_c1_0930.2023.xlsx", "cell_ref": "Report C-1!B6"}], "idb_value": 339965, "variance": 234, "variance_pct": 0.06887802408376038, "tolerance_pct": 0.5, "status": "matched", "explanations": [], "badge": {"status": "matched", "official_value": 339731, "idb_value": 339965, "variance": 234, "variance_pct": 0.06887802408376038, "explanation": null}, "rule": "Cases with an AO filing date in the fiscal year, counted once per case (district, office, docket, filing date)."}, "clarification": null, "provenance": [{"source": "official_table", "table_code": "C-1", "series": "Judicial Business of the United States Courts", "edition": "JB-2023", "period": {"fiscal_year": 2023, "period_end": "2023-09-30", "period_type": "fiscal_year"}, "definition": "Civil cases commenced in the 12-month period (Table C-1, all civil cases).", "url": "https://www.uscourts.gov/sites/default/files/data_tables/jb_c1_0930.2023.xlsx", "cell_ref": "Report C-1!B6", "revision_status": null, "first_published": null, "later_revisions": [], "reconciliation": {"status": "matched", "official_value": 339731, "idb_value": 339965, "variance": 234, "variance_pct": 0.06887802408376038, "explanation": null}, "dataset_release": null, "note": null}, {"source": "idb_derived", "table_code": null, "series": "FJC Integrated Database, civil", "edition": null, "period": null, "definition": "Cases with an AO filing date in the fiscal year, counted once per case (district, office, docket, filing date).", "url": "https://www.fjc.gov/sites/default/files/idb/textfiles/cv88on.zip", "cell_ref": null, "revision_status": null, "first_published": null, "later_revisions": [], "reconciliation": null, "dataset_release": "Wed, 26 Aug 2026 15:28:04 GMT (Cases terminated in SY 1988 through June 30, 2026 and cases pending as of June 30, 2026)", "note": null}], "warnings": [], "suggested_next": []}, "error": null, "latency_s": null}], "extra_outputs": [], "cited_figures": [], "behavior": null, "latency_s": 5.181, "input_tokens": 4, "output_tokens": 314, "error": null}, "score": {"question_id": "ts-reconcile-figure", "suite": "tool_selection", "split": "test", "tags": ["reconcile"], "correct": true, "checks": {"behavior": true, "tools": true}, "expected_behavior": "answer", "actual_behavior": "answer", "error_category": null, "notes": [], "latency_s": 5.181}}
{"question": "What does \"weighted filings\" mean?", "record": {"question_id": "ts-explain-term-weighted", "answerer": "claude-code-sonnet", "final_text": "**Weighted filings** are case filings multiplied by case weights the Federal Judicial Center derives from time studies \u2014 so each case counts based on the relative judge time it typically requires (a death-penalty habeas case weighs far more than a student-loan collection case). Dividing weighted filings by authorized judgeships gives \"weighted filings per judgeship,\" which the Judicial Conference uses to assess judgeship needs. The current weights come from the FJC's 2016 study and are not fully published.\n\nSource: Judicial Business Table X-1A and JFF Table 6.2 notes; FJC.", "tool_calls": [{"name": "explain_term", "arguments": {"term": "weighted filings"}, "output": {"status": "ok", "data": {"query": "weighted filings", "found": true, "definition": {"term": "weighted filings", "kind": "glossary", "definition": "Filings multiplied by case weights the Federal Judicial Center derives from time studies, so each case counts by the relative judge time its type needs (a death-penalty habeas case weighs far more than a student-loan collection). Weighted filings per judgeship divide the weighted total by authorized judgeships. The Judicial Conference uses them to assess judgeship needs. Current weights come from the FJC's 2016 study; the weights themselves are not fully published.", "source": "Judicial Business Table X-1A and JFF Table 6.2 notes; FJC", "related": ["authorized judgeships", "unweighted filings"], "measure_id": "weighted_total_filings_per_judgeship", "nos_code": null, "nos_group": null, "nos_category": null}, "did_you_mean": []}, "clarification": null, "provenance": [{"source": "derived", "table_code": null, "series": null, "edition": null, "period": null, "definition": "Glossary entry, measure definition or codebook label.", "url": null, "cell_ref": null, "revision_status": null, "first_published": null, "later_revisions": [], "reconciliation": null, "dataset_release": null, "note": "Judicial Business Table X-1A and JFF Table 6.2 notes; FJC"}], "warnings": [], "suggested_next": []}, "error": null, "latency_s": null}], "extra_outputs": [], "cited_figures": [], "behavior": null, "latency_s": 5.055, "input_tokens": 4, "output_tokens": 277, "error": null}, "score": {"question_id": "ts-explain-term-weighted", "suite": "tool_selection", "split": "test", "tags": ["glossary"], "correct": true, "checks": {"behavior": true, "tools": true}, "expected_behavior": "answer", "actual_behavior": "answer", "error_category": null, "notes": [], "latency_s": 5.055}}
